# Flourishing Bloom-Kin (Disguise {4}{G}) cast face down with Black Lotus ({3}) is a 2/2 with no abilities (CR 708.2): entering
# triggers nothing. Turned face up for {4}{G} (CR 702.168d, 116.2b) it is a 0/0 that gets +1/+1 for each Forest Bot1 controls
# (CR 613.4c): one, the Forest played this turn, so 1/1. The cost is refused with three sources, none green, and with four, one
# green (a count short), then paid exactly from Forest and four Moxen: the pool is empty right after (`? Bot1.Mana =`).
# "When this creature is turned face up" (CR 701.40b) triggers: Bot1 searches for up to two Forest cards - Bayou, a nonbasic
# Forest, and a Forest - and the Mountain (not a Forest) and three Forests (it is "up to two") are refused. Both are revealed;
# Bot1 puts Bayou onto the battlefield tapped (2 Forests, so 2/2) and the Forest into the hand. Bot2's Forest, in its library
# and then on its battlefield, is untouched and never counted: on turn 3 Bot1 plays the Forest it found and Bloom-Kin is 3/3.

